  "id": "stability",
  "term": "stability",
  "definition": "In diagnosis, stability means how well an initial diagnosis stays the same over time after follow-up. It is clinically meaningful because a stable diagnosis may reflect a brief, self-limited episode, while a changing diagnosis can indicate relapse or the emergence of a different, more persistent disorder.",
